repository-code: https://github.com/itu-itis25-bektes23/ecpm
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An 8-node packet-routing MDP generated in pairs: a world M0 and a copy M1
  carrying at most one recorded intervention. A model reads balanced
  observation logs from both periods and answers four probes: detection,
  localization, preservation and adaptation. Routes are scored by execution
  in the true simulator rather than by the model's own judgment.

  The repository includes an evidence-only baseline, a non-reasoning counter
  that answers the same probes from the same prompt view by arithmetic. It
  establishes, per condition, how much of the task is solvable without
  reasoning, so a model result can be read as above, at, or below what
  counting alone achieves.
keywords:
  - in-context learning
  - change detection
  - world models
  - large language models
  - evaluation
